GitLab CI builds

The first stage has four independent jobs, each with its own artifact archive:
  build-development-image    Development factory image, NAOS_PACKAGE=0.
  build-development-inputs   Development image-generator inputs, NAOS_PACKAGE=1.
  build-production-image     Production factory image, NAOS_PACKAGE=0.
  build-production-inputs    Production image-generator inputs, NAOS_PACKAGE=1.

They use the yocto runner and yocto-runner:ubuntu-24.04-kas as a non-root user.
Jobs in this project are serialized to reuse its Yocto downloads and sstate
cache. Only a numeric MACHINE-X.Y.Z release tag creates a pipeline and starts
all four jobs automatically; the tag helper verifies the selected MACHINE.
Branch pushes do not create pipelines.

The second stage has package-development and package-production. Each downloads
only its matching inputs job's artifacts, not either factory image archive.
It uses apk-builder-runner and seapapa/apkbuild:latest. The two runners do not
share a working directory or Yocto caches.

Build variables
  MACHINE=mixtile-core3588e-v2    Select the board.
  NAOS_OTA=0                    Set 1 to generate system and bootloader OTA bundles.
  NAOS_VERSION, NAOS_BUILD_ID    Optionally set identifiers for non-release builds.

Each CI job fixes its own profile and image/export mode. Local kas builds
retain NAOS_PACKAGE=0. Other feature defaults come from the selected kas
profile. Production enables secure boot, disk encryption and SBOM; development
leaves them disabled.

APK releases
  A tag must exactly match MACHINE-X.Y.Z, for example:
    mixtile-core3588e-v2-1.0.0
  The tag sets the NAOS and APK version to 1.0.0; the APK revision is r0.
  Each package job runs automatically when its matching input build succeeds.
  Branch pipelines do not publish APKs.

The selected apk/development/rk3588/APKBUILD or apk/production/rk3588/APKBUILD
packages the complete verified export without changing its inner files or
archives. The package names distinguish the profiles:
  Development: MACHINE-alpine-dev, for example mixtile-core3588e-v2-alpine-dev.
  Production:  MACHINE-alpine-prod, for example mixtile-core3588e-v2-alpine-prod.
Both packages are published to the same repository directory and index:
  https://packages.naos.ai/repository/x86_64/
The installed export is at /usr/share/naos/image-inputs/PROFILE/MACHINE.
APKBUILD uses arch="all"; the current builder produces x86_64 packages for the
image-generator host. The export's target architecture remains aarch64.
Package jobs publish APKs to the repository and do not retain GitLab artifacts.

The package stage installs Python and the SSH client, builds and verifies the
APK, signs a merged repository index in CI, then uploads the APK and index over
SSH. The server stores the public verification key and publishes the update
atomically; the signing private key remains in CI. Publication checks for
concurrent updates to the common repository index.

Repository variables
  NAOS_APK_REPOSITORY_URL  https://packages.naos.ai/repository
  NAOS_APK_SSH_HOST        56.10.200.210
  NAOS_APK_SSH_USER        ubuntu

The repository variable is the HTTP base address. The publisher appends the
architecture; do not append a profile to NAOS_APK_REPOSITORY_URL.
The public verification key is at https://packages.naos.ai/keys/naos-apk.rsa.pub.
https://www.mixtile.com is the APKBUILD homepage, not the repository endpoint.

CI/CD File variables
  NAOS_CI_OTA_PRIVATE_KEY             OTA signing.key.pem
  NAOS_CI_OTA_CERTIFICATE             OTA signing.cert.pem
  NAOS_CI_SECURE_BOOT_PRIVATE_KEY     Secure boot dev.key
  NAOS_CI_SECURE_BOOT_CERTIFICATE     Secure boot dev.crt
  NAOS_CI_SECURE_BOOT_PUBLIC_KEY      Secure boot dev.pubkey
  NAOS_CI_SYSTEM_KEY                 system.key
  NAOS_CI_SSH_CA_PUBLIC_KEY           ssh_ca_key.pub
  NAOS_CI_APK_SIGNING_KEY            APK repository signing private key
  NAOS_CI_APK_SIGNING_PUBLIC_KEY     naos-apk.rsa.pub
  NAOS_CI_APK_SSH_PRIVATE_KEY        Restricted repository upload SSH private key
  NAOS_CI_APK_SSH_KNOWN_HOSTS        Pinned repository server SSH host key

Configure these in Settings > CI/CD > Variables as protected File variables.
Run builds from a protected branch or tag so the variables are available.
Protect the MACHINE-* release tags before publishing APKs.
system.key must be exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters without a newline.
The OTA certificate is required for every build. Private signing and encryption
inputs are required only when their corresponding build features use them.
Production also requires the SSH CA public key.

The build script stages File variables in a private temporary directory outside
the checkout and removes that directory on exit. Key files are not CI artifacts.

Caches
  DL_DIR defaults to /cache/naos-yocto/${CI_PROJECT_ID}/downloads.
  SSTATE_DIR defaults to /cache/naos-yocto/${CI_PROJECT_ID}/sstate-cache.
  Set either variable to override its default. Build work stays in the job checkout.
  KAS_CLONE_DEPTH defaults to 1 for shallow layer repository checkouts.
  Their pinned commit IDs remain unchanged.

Artifacts contain only firmware, OTA bundles, SBOM files and image-generator
exports that the selected build produced. They expire after one week.
Factory images use .img.zst compression to avoid duplicating A/B payloads in
the artifact archive. Restore the raw image before flashing:
  zstd --long=28 -d naos-mixtile-core3588e-v2.img.zst
